# Anaphora (tasks.org, aida-referents-anaphora; the author's
# tests/anaphora/man.fspy, 2026-10-22). "A plumber walks. A knight walks.
# He whistles." The indefinites introduce individuals (!a, each its
# argument's own); the pronoun owes one (?c). Its witness scaffold tries
# the individuals introduced before it, the latest on top, and keeps one:
# he_whistles evaluates to the knight's reading alone. Its by default is
# about whoever answers, so each reading presumes whistling of its
# candidate. The knight's !a is shown !a_2 in the pronoun's term (the name
# !a is the plumber's there).
lk.
pipeline unfolded.
declare iota : type.
declare knight,plumber,whistles,walks : iota -> bool.
argument plumber_walks : [!a:iota](exists x:iota, plumber [x] - ~walks [x]).
elim [!a].
by default.
dixi.
argument knight_walks : [!a:iota](exists x:iota, knight [x] - ~walks [x]).
elim [!a].
by default.
dixi.
argument he_whistles : [?c:iota](exists x:iota, whistles [x]).
elim [?c].
by default.
dixi.
